00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:02.230 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  it's ps plus time again the extra set of  games each month added for extra and  premium members to enjoy 11 games this  time around which will be yours from  tuesday august 16th we've got a lot to  get through so let's crack on you've  likely heard the news that ps plus will  soon be the home of eight yakuza games  before the end of the year this time  around we have yakuza 0 yakuza kawami  and kawami 2. kiwami is in fact a remake  of the 2005 ps2 game so if you've ever  wanted to play the series from the  beginning you can with modern day polish  we play out the early days of kazuma  kiryu as he returns home after a stint  in prison this action rpg has us  returning to the yakuza underworld after  being blamed for a crime you didn't  commit and now it's time to find answers  kiwami 2 then continues that journey and  yakuza 0 offers a new perspective on all  this as it's a prequel set in the 1980s  from terrible karaoke singing to  collecting debts around the city the  yakuza games these action rpgs are  crammed full of content so much so that  it'll take around 100 hours to get a  platinum in any of these games a day to  try next we have tom clancy's ghost  recon wildlands an open world sandbox of  military possibilities a third-person  tactical shooter from back in 2017. we  arrive at this tropical country and we  are told to take out all the bad guys  controlling this place and then off we  go the game doesn't hold your hand do it  however you choose to alone or with a  team of three friends without a doubt  the best part of wildlands is playing  with your mates timing snipes from  unreal distances watching each other's  back in stealth missions and keeping  each other alive in frantic shootouts  playing with ai just doesn't have the  same feel each province in the wildlands  has a crime lord to find and then take  out which in turn gives us more  information about the boss of those  bosses the game has been updated many  times over the years so watch out if  you're ever walking through the jungle  because the predator lives there this is  no joke it's true at its core wildlands  is yet another rpg with skill points to  gain and unlock different tech which  admittedly does change your play style  so it is worth the grind tom clancy's  ghost recon wildlands is a blast with  the right people around you playing  alone it does get a little boring i have  to admit game 5 is dead by daylight an  asymmetric multiplayer survival game  that continues to receive constant  updates playing as four survivors we  must work together to escape completing  tasks along the way the thing is there's  a maniacal killer on your trail and  their job is to prevent anyone from  escaping at all dead by daylight was  released six years ago and continues to  be the best game in its genre thanks to  its constant updates right now you can  find survivors and killers from  different horror franchises michael  myers is here nancy and steve from  stranger things are here pyramid head  from silent hill is here the game is  packed with horror legends from  different mediums each with a different  level to master both as a hunter and the  prey definitely try dead by daylight if  you haven't already unless this kind of  game scares you of course game six is  bug snacks don't worry this isn't deja  vu it was on ps plus in the past we take  control of a journalist who is summoned  to snacktooth island which so happens to  be the home of bugs that are made out of  food our job is to find where everyone  vanished to and also to catch all those  creatures like edible pokemon with over  100 to find it should take a while as  each critter requires a different  technique to capture bug snacks was a  surprise hit in 2020 and since then the  review score has evened out at about 7  out of 10. game 7 is the greatest game  ever made uno a card game about matching  colors and numbers it's super simple to  learn but really difficult to win if  you're chatting with a group of friends  online this game is perfect for that  without all the hassle of playing with a  real deck of cards the only issue is  playing against ai that's not fun  because the ai never loses game 8 metro  exodus the third metro game based on the  novels of dmitry glykovsky an apocalypse  has devastated the world the thing is  it's all our fault humanity did this  thanks to nukes the game takes place  over a year as the survivors continue  their journey across russia with a harsh  winter rolling in the shooting mechanics  have been refined yet again and the  small dark corridors of the metro are  only one aspect this time around as more  open areas are here freely to explore  making the player decide which direction  is the safest and which will lead to a  fight with irradiated beings metro  exodus reviews at 7 out of 10. game 9 is  something from the 16-bit era trials of  mana has gone from the 2d world into  modern 3d standards this remake remains  an action role-playing game but the  super nintendo limits are no longer an  issue if you've ever played a jrpg like  early final fantasy games this is more  of that kind of goodness and you've  already decided before i even finish  this sentence if you're gonna try it or  not and finally games 10 and 11 are  monopoly madness and monopoly plus  madness takes the base game and  revolutionizes it into a frantic real  estate free-for-all this is all fine  until power-ups are thrown into the mix  drive a bulldozer into someone's hotel  cause a flood to people living near  water and block roads to prevent other  players from buying in your neighborhood  monopoly madness is nothing like the  board game it's crazy and it's actually  a pretty good time with friends monopoly  plus on the other hand is as close to  the base game as it could be the  difference is things move each character  interacts with the environment around  them giving monopoly a new lease of life  so that's august 2022 for ps plus on  extra and premium what are your thoughts  on this i'm adam you're awesome see ya

